resources.string:
PixelWanker helps you check spacing and alignment faster with a clean grid overlay.

👉 the details 👌

PixelWanker is a utility for Android developers and designers who want a fast way to check UI spacing, alignment, and visual rhythm directly on the device.

The app generates a customizable on-screen grid and lets you overlay it on top of any app, so you can instantly evaluate:

- padding and margins between elements;

- spacing inside lists, cards, and screens;

- alignment consistency;

- grid-based layout and overall UI rhythm;

Also useful for web developers shipping mobile experiences (responsive websites, PWAs, WebView-based apps).

Open your site on a phone and use the grid overlay to quickly spot real-device spacing issues that are easy to miss in DevTools:

- inconsistent spacing across breakpoints;

- uneven vertical rhythm (8 / 12 / 16 px systems);

- misaligned icons and text baselines;

- tap-target spacing and layout “drift” on small screens;

Key features:

- Grid overlay on top of any app (overlay).

- Adjustable cell size for the level of precision you need (px / dp).

- Custom grid color for visibility on any background.

- Quick UI checks without taking screenshots or using external editors.

For pixel-perfect enthusiasts, Pixel wanker for Android dev helps you lock in spacing quickly and reduce back-and-forth iterations — whether you’re polishing a native Android UI or fine-tuning a mobile web layout on a real device.
